  "content": {
    "id": "p17-q4-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "Suppose a chessboard were to have rice placed upon each square such that one grain is placed on the first square, three on the second square, nine on the third square, and so on (tripling the number of grains on each subsequent square). How many grains of rice would be on the chessboard in total?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\dfrac{3^{64}-1}{2}=1\\,716\\,841\\,910\\,146\\,256\\,242\\,328\\,924\\,544\\,640$ grains.",
      "worked": "A chessboard has 64 squares. The numbers of grains form a geometric sequence with $a=1$ and $r=3$.\n$$\\begin{align*}S_{64}&=1+3+3^2+\\cdots+3^{63}\\\\S_{64}&=\\frac{1(3^{64}-1)}{3-1}\\\\S_{64}&=\\frac{3^{64}-1}{2}\\\\S_{64}&=1\\,716\\,841\\,910\\,146\\,256\\,242\\,328\\,924\\,544\\,640.\\end{align*}$$\nThe chessboard contains $1\\,716\\,841\\,910\\,146\\,256\\,242\\,328\\,924\\,544\\,640$ grains in total.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 43
  },
